      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "A forex trader's annual profits have been *growing* continuously at a rate of $7\\%$ per year. Her profit this year is $\\$13700$. What was her profit $5$ years ago? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the continuously compounded growth equation $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The current amount is $P=13700$, the rate is $r=0.07$ (positive for growth), and the elapsed time is $t=5$ years. The time unit matches the rate. Substitute and divide by the exponential factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n13700 &= P_0e^{(0.07)(5)} \\\\\n13700 &= P_0e^{0.35} \\\\\ne^{0.35} &\\approx 1.41906755 \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{13700}{e^{0.35}} \\\\\n&\\approx 9654\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe earlier profit was $\\$9654$. Round only the final amount; keep full calculator precision in the exponential factor.",
